 padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Considering how he raised the Veil between the world and the Fade, I would think his role is closer to Father Wolf than a Firstborn.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:11:56-07:00","id":991677,"title":"","content":"Good point. In retrospect that should have been the obvious parallel to draw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T21:07:13-07:00","id":991698,"title":"","content":"I would think that the Taxonomies of early mage would not be as refined as they are now, so perhaps they weren't making the distinctions between realms so much.<br /> <br /> Though I've never drawn this parallel as DA lacks paradox AFAIK (that said, sometimes I hate paradox as a general risk, seems like one of those mechanics generally designed to hide supernaturals from the world, if we didn't have it stuff would be all over youtube). Also, Fae aside, I would say that ChroD lacks elves, and dwarves aren't a race (but a condition). I just thought DA was a better D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 10-23-2016, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T21:34:27-07:00","id":991705,"title":"","content":"While ChroD does lack elves, dwarves, and qunari, engineering rulesets for the races isn't too hard.<br /> <br /> Use the system presented in mirrors to fabricate races. Atlaneans more or less fill the elf niche in ChroD in terms of setup, but we may want to go further to allow our DA elves to be more respentive. But these should be rather easy I feel.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I feel I disagree. Dwarves are a valid race, especially if there's unique traits to them that are not merely physical... In the case of DA. We're looking at some sort of magic resistance ability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:28:53-07:00","id":991725,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't see lack of fantasy races as any barrier at all, considering the whole point is to make a fantasy Shard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:33:35-07:00","id":991877,"title":"","content":"Well, what kind of racial traits you'd put for them?<br /> <br /> <br /> For the Qunari, I think we'd need to make note of their physicality being so much above the human norms. Yet I don't know of an appropriate biodrawback to give them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dwarves can obviously cash in on reducing the potency of magical effects and toxins used against them. Something like a -1 reduction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Elves apparently gain missile defense of some sort in Inquisition... so maybe a bonus to defense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:47:10-07:00","id":991903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991877#post991877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Qunari, I think we'd need to make note of their physicality being so much above the human norms. Yet I don't know of an appropriate biodrawback to give them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Base size 6 seems like an appropriate bonus, and needing to have clothing and armor made to fit the larger stature and potentially horns seems like a fine drawback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991877#post991877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dwarves can obviously cash in on reducing the potency of magical effects and toxins used against them. Something like a -1 reduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dwarves might be tough, cause not being able to be Mages seems like a pretty big drawback, only made worse by using Awakening's magic system. What if Dwarves accelerate Dissonance or something? Maybe a bonus to Withstand spells?<br /> <br /> It's hard cause the Sleeping Curse and Paradox don't really have a close equivalent in Dragon Age. Unless you count the Blight? Maybe it's an Abyssal plague and magic spreads it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991877#post991877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elves apparently gain missile defense of some sort in Inquisition... so maybe a bonus to defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they retain the higher of Wits or Dexterity to Defense against Archery (but still lose Athletics)? Too strong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-23-2016, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:24:24-07:00","id":991946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991903#post991903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Base size 6 seems like an appropriate bonus, and needing to have clothing and armor made to fit the larger stature and potentially horns seems like a fine drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose +1 to any availability things. I guess?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dwarves might be tough, cause not being able to be Mages seems like a pretty big drawback, only made worse by using Awakening's magic system. What if Dwarves accelerate Dissonance or something? Maybe a bonus to Withstand spells?<br /> <br /> It's hard cause the Sleeping Curse and Paradox don't really have a close equivalent in Dragon Age. Unless you count the Blight? Maybe it's an Abyssal plague and magic<br /> spreads it... </div> </div> </div>Well, the other issue is that... DA magic is more limited in many ways than Awakening magic, since it seems to lack quite a bit Time, Fate, and Space manipulation.<br /> You could perhaps consider maybe borrowing Hedgemage rules and adapting them. Most of the mages we see tend to be brute force &quot;blasters&quot; who can cause destructive magic and some support here and there. Some medicines, healers, enchanters, but we're talking all small fry.<br /> <br /> Save the Awakened magic for &quot;important&quot; people, like say Hawke or Corpy. They tend to be head and shoulders above the normal crowd and have more flexible applications of magic. While training perhaps goes into explaining the discrepancy, that doesn't work for say, all of the rogue mages. You'd have to also bear in mind that you need to make the Templars stronger proportionally in order for them to matter against Awakened if all DA mages were Awakened since there's always been that balance of power. Seperating common mages from true mages goes a long way to making it easier to justify Templar close to what we see. Possibly make an Endowment for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the purposes of Dwarves... let's just say that whenever they have to do anything to resist magic, regardless of what type it is, it is treated as 1 &quot;level&quot; weaker. And they can't be magically inclined.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe they retain the higher of Wits or Dexterity to Defense against Archery (but still lose Athletics)? Too strong? </div> </div> </div>Maybe lower of Wits or Dex. Still lose Athletics. The defense bonus in Inquisition is 25% resistance against all missile attacks (including magical ones apparently). <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and on the topic of magic. I made this ages ago, partly because of DA, partly because of Ziggarut to make generalized magic weapons. Will this be of any value to you? This can be used to explain why most mages are only blasters.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865817-homebrew-generic-magical-weapons-wands-staves-books\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865817-homebrew-generic-magical-weapons-wands-staves-books\"> [Homebrew] Generic Magical Weapons: Wands, Staves, Books - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865817-homebrew-generic-magical-weapons-wands-staves-books\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865817-homebrew-generic-magical-weapons-wands-staves-books </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This is a sort of&hellip;. side project that I wanted to come up with. Wanted to do it because&hellip; I saw no one else offering a similar thing outside of obviously Mages </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:36:31-07:00","id":992017,"title":"","content":"I'd like to recommend an alternative: Run each species and class as a major splat, instead of a merit-based template addition. This will involve packing away the supernatural creatures from ChroD but might result in a more interesting game (and could give you some interesting implications about each class and species) [I say species because there's no evidence in Dragon Age that the different &quot;races&quot; are genetically compatible; you never see a half-dwarf, half-elf, or whatever].<br /> <br /> We'll start with Dwarves. Due to their penchant for alchemy and their restriction from magic, I'd recommend running them with the Promethean book. Make disquiet specifically and exclusively affect mages, and perhaps attach a potency reducer to it based on the stage experienced.<br /> <br /> Elves, particularly the Dalish, would benefit from being run by the Werewolf book. Their dedication to the spirits (many of which are revered as gods in their society) and their connection to the Fade (which contains the Shadow if you're using the &quot;break upon the fall&quot; model) feels like a good fit. Snip around the shapeshifting unless the elf also happens to be a mage.<br /> <br /> The Vashoth I'd create using the Changeling book, with the Qunari serving explicitly as the True Fae. The Qun is a harsh philosophy not above stealing people away from their lives for service, which makes this an appropriate fit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humans are trickier. I'd be inclined to split humans across different books based on what class they choose.<br /> <br /> I'd run Templars with the Vampire book. Lyrium is actually a living mineral, and...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Red lyrium is lyrium infected with the blight</div></div> </div> </div><br /> so simulating the magic halting power of a templar with the blood suckers feels par for the course. Keep in mind Templars stop magic by widening the veil with their training; Lyrium just facilitates that mental control. It IS magic in that it is anti-magic. I'd also say lower the potency of magic against templars as you would against a dwarf. Double for a dwarf templar (only the player ever attained this combination in canon, but it is hypothetically possible).<br /> Other Warriors would be built with the Heroic Mortal template from Mirrors. Emphasize the extra health levels in particular.<br /> <br /> I'd run Rogues with the Geist book. Something about manifestations screams ambush preparation to me; you can strip away some of the magical components of these ghost powers and make them into exploitation of terrain instead. The Boneyard manifestation is particularly appropriate in this regard. Also, delaying injuries but then succumbing to them later is such a rogue thing to do. Instead of Plasm for this, make them use herbalism to gather poisons for the purpose of attaining the same effects.<br /> <br /> Mages are tricky. As has been stated upthread, the Awakened in the Mage book are seriously powerful entities and it may be best to reserve the splat for big figures in the world.<br /> Since Dragon Age Mages have the potential to 'pupate' into horrible abominations, I'd say make them with the Demon book (and make &quot;Going Loud&quot; the mutate part).<br /> <br /> As for other major players...<br /> I'd make Flemeth with the Mummy book. Primarily because:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">She starts off incredibly powerful, but gradually degrades and must reincarnate in a stolen daughter to regain her might</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And as for the Archdemon, I'd make it with the Beast book. While you might be inclined to make it as a spirit or not stat it at all, the Archdemon has been killed at least five times in the Dragon Age universe and so much exist as a slayable entity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, if you do this you might end up blurring some template lines, particularly with dwarven and elven rogues (who would need to be able to at least purchase Manifestations). Still, it might be worth consideration... at least to shrink the power disparity your current model presents with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:38:54-07:00","id":992020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991946#post991946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose +1 to any availability things. I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess that works. Could probably be refined a bit, but it's a start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991946#post991946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the other issue is that... DA magic is more limited in many ways than Awakening magic, since it seems to lack quite a bit Time, Fate, and Space manipulation.<br /> You could perhaps consider maybe borrowing Hedgemage rules and adapting them. Most of the mages we see tend to be brute force &amp;quot;blasters&amp;quot; who can cause destructive magic and some support here and there. Some medicines, healers, enchanters, but we're talking all small fry.<br /> <br /> Save the Awakened magic for &amp;quot;important&amp;quot; people, like say Hawke or Corpy. They tend to be head and shoulders above the normal crowd and have more flexible applications of magic. While training perhaps goes into explaining the discrepancy, that doesn't work for say, all of the rogue mages. You'd have to also bear in mind that you need to make the Templars stronger proportionally in order for them to matter against Awakened if all DA mages were Awakened since there's always been that balance of power. Seperating common mages from true mages goes a long way to making it easier to justify Templar close to what we see. Possibly make an Endowment for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all true. I suppose I just assumed DA Mages would be Awakened because of how a lot of similar themes are emphasized - &quot;Magic Should Serve Man, not Rule Over Him&quot; is very much in line with the concepts behind Wisdom, and a big part of the reason people feel Templars are necessary is fear of what Mages are capable of, which always sort of reminded me of the &quot;Mage supremacy&quot; complaints. But yeah, it is pretty tough to reconcile the differences, so maybe only the really powerful ones should be Mages.<br /> <br /> Also, my first instinct upon reading Hawke as an example of a powerful Mage was &quot;What? Hawke was a rogue...&quot; Then I remembered my Hawke is not everyone's Hawke ::blush::<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991946#post991946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the purposes of Dwarves... let's just say that whenever they have to do anything to resist magic, regardless of what type it is, it is treated as 1 &amp;quot;level&amp;quot; weaker. And they can't be magically inclined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... Still feels unsatisfying to me. I always find flat bonuses and penalties kind of boring as template abilities. Even just letting them substitute Stamina for any one other Trait when resisting magical effects or something feels more impactful to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991946#post991946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe lower of Wits or Dex. Still lose Athletics. The defense bonus in Inquisition is 25% resistance against all missile attacks (including magical ones apparently).</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh! I meant to type lower. Yeah, that feels pretty good to me. It'd apply against any ranged attacks that normally ignore Defense, like Archery and aimed spells with the Fast Spells Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=991946#post991946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and on the topic of magic. I made this ages ago, partly because of DA, partly because of Ziggarut to make generalized magic weapons. Will this be of any value to you? This can be used to explain why most mages are only blasters.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865817-homebrew-generic-magical-weapons-wands-staves-books\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865817-homebrew-generic-magical-weapons-wands-staves-books\"> [Homebrew] Generic Magical Weapons: Wands, Staves, Books - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865817-homebrew-generic-magical-weapons-wands-staves-books\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865817-homebrew-generic-magical-weapons-wands-staves-books </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This is a sort of&hellip;. side project that I wanted to come up with. Wanted to do it because&hellip; I saw no one else offering a similar thing outside of obviously Mages </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possibly! I'll take a look ASAP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:49:32-07:00","id":992031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992017#post992017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to recommend an alternative: Run each species and class as a major splat, instead of a merit-based template addition. This will involve packing away the supernatural creatures from ChroD but might result in a more interesting game (and could give you some interesting implications about each class and species) [I say species because there's no evidence in Dragon Age that the different &amp;quot;races&amp;quot; are genetically compatible; you never see a half-dwarf, half-elf, or whatever].</div> </div> </div> </div>Fanriel is a half-elf. They seem to be pretty rare, but they do exist. And it's hinted Qunari and Vashoth might actually be the result of careful selective breeding, possibly including Dragon somewhere in there. Dwarves might very well be a different species though, that would explain their different relationship with the Fade than the other &quot;races&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992017#post992017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll start with Dwarves. Due to their penchant for alchemy and their restriction from magic, I'd recommend running them with the Promethean book. Make disquiet specifically and exclusively affect mages, and perhaps attach a potency reducer to it based on the stage experienced.<br /> <br /> Elves, particularly the Dalish, would benefit from being run by the Werewolf book. Their dedication to the spirits (many of which are revered as gods in their society) and their connection to the Fade (which contains the Shadow if you're using the &amp;quot;break upon the fall&amp;quot; model) feels like a good fit. Snip around the shapeshifting unless the elf also happens to be a mage.<br /> <br /> The Vashoth I'd create using the Changeling book, with the Qunari serving explicitly as the True Fae. The Qun is a harsh philosophy not above stealing people away from their lives for service, which makes this an appropriate fit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humans are trickier. I'd be inclined to split humans across different books based on what class they choose.<br /> <br /> I'd run Templars with the Vampire book. Lyrium is actually a living mineral, and...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Red lyrium is lyrium infected with the blight</div></div> </div> </div><br /> so simulating the magic halting power of a templar with the blood suckers feels par for the course. Keep in mind Templars stop magic by widening the veil with their training; Lyrium just facilitates that mental control. It IS magic in that it is anti-magic. I'd also say lower the potency of magic against templars as you would against a dwarf. Double for a dwarf templar (only the player ever attained this combination in canon, but it is hypothetically possible).<br /> Other Warriors would be built with the Heroic Mortal template from Mirrors. Emphasize the extra health levels in particular.<br /> <br /> I'd run Rogues with the Geist book. Something about manifestations screams ambush preparation to me; you can strip away some of the magical components of these ghost powers and make them into exploitation of terrain instead. The Boneyard manifestation is particularly appropriate in this regard. Also, delaying injuries but then succumbing to them later is such a rogue thing to do. Instead of Plasm for this, make them use herbalism to gather poisons for the purpose of attaining the same effects.<br /> <br /> Mages are tricky. As has been stated upthread, the Awakened in the Mage book are seriously powerful entities and it may be best to reserve the splat for big figures in the world.<br /> Since Dragon Age Mages have the potential to 'pupate' into horrible abominations, I'd say make them with the Demon book (and make &amp;quot;Going Loud&amp;quot; the mutate part).<br /> <br /> As for other major players...<br /> I'd make Flemeth with the Mummy book. Primarily because:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">She starts off incredibly powerful, but gradually degrades and must reincarnate in a stolen daughter to regain her might</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And as for the Archdemon, I'd make it with the Beast book. While you might be inclined to make it as a spirit or not stat it at all, the Archdemon has been killed at least five times in the Dragon Age universe and so much exist as a slayable entity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, if you do this you might end up blurring some template lines, particularly with dwarven and elven rogues (who would need to be able to at least purchase Manifestations). Still, it might be worth consideration... at least to shrink the power disparity your current model presents with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting ideas. This is definitely not the way I would go with it because that's a lot more reskinning than I would want to do. ChroD mechanics are generally very closely tied to the narrative, the fluff/crunch line is super blurry and at least one of the developers has explicitly stated that he doesn't subscribe to the idea of a fluff/crunch divide, game content is game content. I tend to agree with him, at least when it comes to ChroD. That said, I do like the idea of making some things (such as Templars) a full-blown Template instead of just minor tweaking. Either way, thanks for the feedback!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:09:12-07:00","id":992045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992020#post992020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, my first instinct upon reading Hawke as an example of a powerful Mage was &quot;What? Hawke was a rogue...&quot; Then I remembered my Hawke is not everyone's Hawke ::blush::</div> </div> </div> </div>Canonically, well as canon as the trailers are.<br /> The Hero of Ferelden was a Noble Warrior, male.<br /> Hawk was a male Apostate of the default face.<br /> And the Inquisitor is a rogue. Also male human despite Qunari being added as playable.<br /> <br /> This is similar to how Shephard is always a male soldier in Mass Effect despite getting SO MUCH custom material<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jlACgYHtWCI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jlACgYHtWCI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jlACgYHtWCI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jlACgYHtWCI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm... Still feels unsatisfying to me. I always find flat bonuses and penalties kind of boring as template abilities. Even just letting them substitute Stamina for any one other Trait when resisting magical effects or something feels more impactful to me. </div> </div> </div>It's starting thing that I'm extrapolating from the 10% magic resist. We can probably be more creative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doh! I meant to type lower. Yeah, that feels pretty good to me. It'd apply against any ranged attacks that normally ignore Defense, like Archery and aimed spells with the Fast Spells Merit. </div> </div> </div>Let's call it... &quot;Elvish Reflexes&quot;. I guess? What's the downside?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quite possibly! I'll take a look ASAP. </div> </div> </div>It's just a weapons compendium really for making custom &quot;magic weapons&quot;. Not exactly ideal, but translating some of that material might be handy.<br /> <br /> In my experience with DA, Staves are a must for mages so that came to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-23-2016, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:46:32-07:00","id":992075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992045#post992045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically, well as canon as the trailers are.<br /> The Hero of Ferelden was a Noble Warrior, male.<br /> Hawk was a male Apostate of the default face.<br /> And the Inquisitor is a rogue. Also male human despite Qunari being added as playable.<br /> <br /> This is similar to how Shephard is always a male soldier in Mass Effect despite getting SO MUCH custom material</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know. But I'm very attached to my Hawke, trailers be damned. Actually all of my PCs deviate pretty significantly from trailer canon. I just thought it was funny that my instinct was to be like &quot;uh, she's not a Mage?&quot; and then remembering that he or she can be anything and the closest thing to canon does have him as a Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992045#post992045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> IIt's starting thing that I'm extrapolating from the 10% magic resist. We can probably be more creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. Definitely some kind of magic resistance, either way,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992045#post992045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ILet's call it... &quot;Elvish Reflexes&quot;. I guess? What's the downside?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Well, people don't seem to like elves very much, be they wild and mysterious Dalish or dirty knife-eared street rats. Maybe their starting Impressions in Social Maneuvering are one step lower with non-elves?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992045#post992045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just a weapons compendium really for making custom &quot;magic weapons&quot;. Not exactly ideal, but translating some of that material might be handy.<br /> <br /> In my experience with DA, Staves are a must for mages so that came to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Could be useful, for sure. Sorry I'm being brief, on mobile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-23-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:26:51-07:00","id":992118,"title":"","content":"While it's not super-interesting, a flat +1 Withstand for Dwarves would be a pretty decent benefit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:46:23-07:00","id":992127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eggs Maledict</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992118#post992118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's not super-interesting, a flat +1 Withstand for Dwarves would be a pretty decent benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So then the question becomes... do we also want Dwarven magic resistance to apply to magical effects asside from those in Awakening. As far as I am aware, Withstand is a mechanic that's mage specific, so does it have relevance outside of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:58:09-07:00","id":992131,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about how you'd handle warrior/rogue builds and have them not be outclassed by mage powers. Skill tricks, maybe, or Discipline-style powers to partly simulate the skill tree format of the DA games. Powers like celerity, potency, and fortitude seem like a natural fit for rogues and warriors respectively. You could make a character's level in professional expertise the cap for their powers, and maybe have a &quot;prestige&quot; profession that unlocks once their standard expertise level is maxed?<br /> <br /> Also, if you're looking to actually run a Dragon Age game, I hear the existing book is actually pretty damn good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-23-2016, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:25:51-07:00","id":992145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992131#post992131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about how you'd handle warrior/rogue builds and have them not be outclassed by mage powers. Skill tricks, maybe, or Discipline-style powers to partly simulate the skill tree format of the DA games. Powers like celerity, potency, and fortitude seem like a natural fit for rogues and warriors respectively. You could make a character's level in professional expertise the cap for their powers, and maybe have a &amp;quot;prestige&amp;quot; profession that unlocks once their standard expertise level is maxed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm pretty ok with Mages being overpowered. It's pretty much DA canon that they are, that's a big part of the reason for the Circles of Magi. And they worked as long as the Mages were cooperating, but once they decided they weren't going to put up with it any more, the Templars couldn't actually stop them without turning to red Lyrium. I feel like the whole state of affairs in Dragon Age is much more believable if Warriors and Rogues actually aren't a match for equally skilled Mages, without some kind of magical aid like Lyrium like the Templars do or merging with a spirit like the Seekers do. And obviously that doesn't work in the video games, but in Tabletop I think that kind of imbalance can work.<br /> <br /> That said, I think I would make a template or templates for folks who get special abilities from sources other than magic, like Templars and Seekers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992131#post992131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you're looking to actually run a Dragon Age game, I hear the existing book is actually pretty damn good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, if I really wanted to run a DA game I'd probably just use the official RPG. I played the QuickStart and it was a lot of fun. This isn't for a game I have plans of running, more of a theorycrafting &quot;how would DA work in ChroD?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:29:52-07:00","id":992244,"title":"","content":"To be fair, alot of the reason why Heroic Nonmages are able to compete at all is in large part due to their gear. We have good reason to believe that said equipment is stupidly enchanted and augmented. Said system would mitigate some of the drawbacks of being merely mundane...<br /> <br /> There's also applying the idea of some humans just being superhuman... Now, true mages are still freakishly powerful even compared to them, but that doesn't mean said humans aren't without ways to defend themselves....<br /> <br /> In theory, the Dark Hero or an augmented version of that would help define said archetypes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from that, Grey Wardens are hinted at being somewhat more powerful than normal humans due to the taint affecting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-24-2016, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:51:51-07:00","id":992252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992145#post992145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm pretty ok with Mages being overpowered. It's pretty much DA canon that they are, that's a big part of the reason for the Circles of Magi. And they worked as long as the Mages were cooperating, but once they decided they weren't going to put up with it any more, the Templars couldn't actually stop them without turning to red Lyrium. I feel like the whole state of affairs in Dragon Age is much more believable if Warriors and Rogues actually aren't a match for equally skilled Mages, without some kind of magical aid like Lyrium like the Templars do or merging with a spirit like the Seekers do. And obviously that doesn't work in the video games, but in Tabletop I think that kind of imbalance can work.<br /> <br /> That said, I think I would make a template or templates for folks who get special abilities from sources other than magic, like Templars and Seekers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I think we may come from two different viewpoints: you're more interested in the lore, and I'm more interested in the power fantasy of the game. I played the first two, and a big part of the appeal for me is that you and your rag tag crew of vagabonds can rip their way through death cultists, ancient witches, and dragons. I think if you don't have power sets that simulate shadow flickering behind a giant ogre and bursting them down a flurry of strikes or tanking down a flock of demons, you're missing a lot of the visceral appeal of the games themselves. Part of that can be simulated with a more robust approach to equipment, but I think you're missing out on some of the appeal if non-magic users don't have skill trick or dot based powers to simulate their battle advantages.<br /> <br /> As for mages, my feeling is that they're scary to everyday humans, but less so to the heroes that populate the world. The whole game dynamic is about developing from a nobody schmuck into one of the most powerful beings around, and that's never been gated according to whether or not you have access to magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T22:56:46-07:00","id":992269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992252#post992252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. I think we may come from two different viewpoints: you're more interested in the lore, and I'm more interested in the power fantasy of the game. I played the first two, and a big part of the appeal for me is that you and your rag tag crew of vagabonds can rip their way through death cultists, ancient witches, and dragons. I think if you don't have power sets that simulate shadow flickering behind a giant ogre and bursting them down a flurry of strikes or tanking down a flock of demons, you're missing a lot of the visceral appeal of the games themselves. Part of that can be simulated with a more robust approach to equipment, but I think you're missing out on some of the appeal if non-magic users don't have skill trick or dot based powers to simulate their battle advantages.<br /> <br /> As for mages, my feeling is that they're scary to everyday humans, but less so to the heroes that populate the world. The whole game dynamic is about developing from a nobody schmuck into one of the most powerful beings around, and that's never been gated according to whether or not you have access to magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I'll back Dx on that. If you've seen that one DA film, it's not hard to come to the conclusion that their standards of normal humans are very different. Granted, I might be over exaggerating their effectiveness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-24-2016, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T22:58:22-07:00","id":992270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992252#post992252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I think we may come from two different viewpoints: you're more interested in the lore, and I'm more interested in the power fantasy of the game. I played the first two, and a big part of the appeal for me is that you and your rag tag crew of vagabonds can rip their way through death cultists, ancient witches, and dragons. I think if you don't have power sets that simulate shadow flickering behind a giant ogre and bursting them down a flurry of strikes or tanking down a flock of demons, you're missing a lot of the visceral appeal of the games themselves. Part of that can be simulated with a more robust approach to equipment, but I think you're missing out on some of the appeal if non-magic users don't have skill trick or dot based powers to simulate their battle advantages.<br /> <br /> As for mages, my feeling is that they're scary to everyday humans, but less so to the heroes that populate the world. The whole game dynamic is about developing from a nobody schmuck into one of the most powerful beings around, and that's never been gated according to whether or not you have access to magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. I definitely am more into the lore. That, and the interpersonal stories, which is why 2 is still probably my favorite. Although the power fantasy is definitely an appealing part of the video games. Definitely not something I would be interested in carrying over to ChroD. That's kind of the opposite of what ChroD is built for, horror game and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-24-2016, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:13:10-07:00","id":992372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992270#post992270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For sure. I definitely am more into the lore. That, and the interpersonal stories, which is why 2 is still probably my favorite. Although the power fantasy is definitely an appealing part of the video games. Definitely not something I would be interested in carrying over to ChroD. That's kind of the opposite of what ChroD is built for, horror game and all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The two don't have to be mutually seperate, do they? There's lots of things horrible in DA... things that you can fight and face... and things you can kill... and then there's the things you can't... no matter how much power you have.<br /> <br /> <br /> Power, simply adds flavors and different types of horror, rather than taking it away. The horror of impotence for instance worse best when you have a capability... only to realize it isn't worth enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any event:<br /> <br /> Hypothetical minisplat is perhaps a neccesity for this when disccussing heroic normals able to compete with the supernatural?<br /> I'm thinking... we borrow from DA2's layout, have people be able to choose a prestige class later on somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:37:33-07:00","id":992378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992270#post992270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For sure. I definitely am more into the lore. That, and the interpersonal stories, which is why 2 is still probably my favorite. Although the power fantasy is definitely an appealing part of the video games. Definitely not something I would be interested in carrying over to ChroD. That's kind of the opposite of what ChroD is built for, horror game and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same, but I think we're in the minority here.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;epic Tolkien quest&quot; element of DA1 didn't really appeal to me, but the more vignette-driven elements to DA2 did. It's the same reason why Mass Effect 2 was my favorite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992372#post992372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The two don't have to be mutually seperate, do they? There's lots of things horrible in DA... things that you can fight and face... and things you can kill... and then there's the things you can't... no matter how much power you have.<br /> <br /> <br /> Power, simply adds flavors and different types of horror, rather than taking it away. The horror of impotence for instance worse best when you have a capability... only to realize it isn't worth enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any event:<br /> <br /> Hypothetical minisplat is perhaps a neccesity for this when disccussing heroic normals able to compete with the supernatural?<br /> I'm thinking... we borrow from DA2's layout, have people be able to choose a prestige class later on somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think DA is inherently an epic fantasy setting with a lot of potential for epic horror. You need some way to distinguish heroes from everyday humans, and I'm not sure a larger buy-in to the five point attribute/skill system achieves that. Moreover, I think you're missing out if you don't find some way to simulate the class system of the games. That might involve skill tricks, class-based merits, or out-and-out dot powers. I'd maybe take a look at the canon characters and examine what sort of rules you'd need to properly simulate characters like Leriana or Varrick in the game.<br /> <br /> I think, from a balance perspective, you're risking the jedi effect of pre-FFG Star Wars games. A system like this would allow you to play a group that's all Circle Magi or all ordinaries, but the idea of a mixed team just wouldn't be that much fun for players who aren't mages, and a team of ordinaries would be relegated to doing little more than killing rats in basements. I'd probably take the professional expertise merit adapted from Vigil, up the cost, and buff up the advantages you get from it: more meaningful additions like flat attribute boosts and additional merits as you climb up the ladder. Max out your expertise, find a mentor, and you can buy into specialization expertise. Or maybe make your character &quot;level&quot; a 10-point dot system, tied into something similar to ambitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-24-2016, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:06:48-07:00","id":992442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992378#post992378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same, but I think we're in the minority here.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;epic Tolkien quest&quot; element of DA1 didn't really appeal to me, but the more vignette-driven elements to DA2 did. It's the same reason why Mass Effect 2 was my favorite.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, I think DA is inherently an epic fantasy setting with a lot of potential for epic horror. You need some way to distinguish heroes from everyday humans, and I'm not sure a larger buy-in to the five point attribute/skill system achieves that. Moreover, I think you're missing out if you don't find some way to simulate the class system of the games. That might involve skill tricks, class-based merits, or out-and-out dot powers. I'd maybe take a look at the canon characters and examine what sort of rules you'd need to properly simulate characters like Leriana or Varrick in the game.<br /> <br /> I think, from a balance perspective, you're risking the jedi effect of pre-FFG Star Wars games. A system like this would allow you to play a group that's all Circle Magi or all ordinaries, but the idea of a mixed team just wouldn't be that much fun for players who aren't mages, and a team of ordinaries would be relegated to doing little more than killing rats in basements. I'd probably take the professional expertise merit adapted from Vigil, up the cost, and buff up the advantages you get from it: more meaningful additions like flat attribute boosts and additional merits as you climb up the ladder. Max out your expertise, find a mentor, and you can buy into specialization expertise. Or maybe make your character &quot;level&quot; a 10-point dot system, tied into something similar to ambitions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, on thinking on it. We need to seperate Awakened Mages from lower case mages, in the first place don't we? We can't simply have all mages be Mages since the difference in abilities... and the gulf of weaknesses is rather different.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, a universal splat to work as the basis for all of the various niches and roles for heroic characters is a worthwhile solution.<br /> <br /> <br /> Employ the talent tree like system DA 2 uses, fill it in with abilities.<br /> <br /> Have a 1-10 Level thing to represent points of &quot;mana&quot; or &quot;stamina&quot; and you're good to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:26:51-07:00","id":992912,"title":"","content":"Not much time, but what about using Hurt Lock style &quot;micro templates&quot; for races and/or classes? There is a base Merit that serves as foundation and prerequisite for other refining merits.<br /> <br /> To make it more &quot;class-y&quot;, what about setting up Classes as a Condition (like the Demon Agendas) that grants class-specific Beats for behaving in a class-typical manner. The Condition itself might also give certain effects on its own. Let &quot;Class Experiences&quot; be spent on certain Merits (making said class able to acquire them easier/faster), or even restricting certain Merits/abilities to only be acquired with Class Experiences (like Mage 2E Arcane Experience and Gnosis, I think).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:31:32-07:00","id":992915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991514-dragon-age-as-a-fantasy-shard?p=992442#post992442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have a 1-10 Level thing to represent points of &quot;mana&quot; or &quot;stamina&quot; and you're good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about just Willpower? Warriors/Rogues use Stamina, Mages use Mana, but they are basically the same thing mechanically - a consumable, replenishable resource. Willpower already does that.<br /> <br /> If necessary to break things up (because you don't want warriors or rogues dependent upon Resolve + Composure for their mojo pool), I'd still suggest using a similar system. Maybe with more restore or faster spending options, if needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}